' ============================================================================
' 43 The evaluation order of a TensorLogic program.
'
' Source of Figure TL10 in ../tensor-logic/dynamic-semantics.md (section 5.2).
' The figure restates EVALUATE of that section and the recursion classes of
' static-semantics.md section 7. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. The evaluator keeps only the query slice: the statements that the
'      queries need.
'   2. It evaluates the strongly connected components of the slice in
'      topological order, so every tensor that a component reads is final.
'   3. Each component runs by its class: R0 once, R1 by its guard index in
'      ascending order, R2 by semi-naive iteration, stratum by stratum.
'   4. The outputs are encoded in the value ABI, and each element is
'      reserved before it is written.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 43-tl-evaluation-order.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 43-tl-evaluation-order
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam PartitionBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The evaluation order of a TensorLogic program (EVALUATE)

start
:the checked normal form, the inputs
and the precision p; <<$rrs_tl_term>>
:the query slice: the statements
that the queries need (section 6); <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
:the strongly connected components of the slice,
in topological order; <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
while (a component C is left?) is (yes)
  switch (the class of C)
  case (R0: no cycle)
    :evaluate each statement of C once; <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
  case (R1: index-guarded)
    :for g in the domain of the guard, ascending:
    evaluate the statements of C at g
    every read is at a value below g, so it is final; <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
    note right
      A virtual dimension keeps only the
      slices g and g + 1, with the backing
      reserved once.
    end note
  case (R2: Boolean monotone)
    :SEMI-NAIVE(C), stratum by stratum
    (Figure TL11); <<$rrs_tl_engine>>
  endswitch
endwhile (no)
:encode the query outputs in the value ABI,
and reserve each element before it is written; <<$rrs_meter>>
:the outputs; <<$rrs_tl_term>>
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_tl_term>   | TL terms and values |
|<$rrs_tl_engine> | a step of EVALUATE |
|<$rrs_meter>     | a reservation on the host-work meter |
endlegend
@enduml
